//
// Description: This script shows how to read a device and evaulate the return automatically by definng the correct output
//
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Connect to equipment
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1


#2: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM 

Returned result is = %BENUM%
IF: %BENUM% STR_EQ BL1,BL2,BR1,BR2,FL1,FL2,FR1,FR2,RS,RS1,RS2, //  a correct expected Return result 
GOTO: #2.1: // if line 30 and 31 results match goto next test
.
The returned result is NOT as exected, investigate the fault and click RETRY to repeat the test.
.
.
The expected result is = BL1,BL2,BR1,BR2,FL1,FL2,FR1,FR2,RS,RS1,RS2, 
IMPORTANT: Test has FAILED                Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED
COMMENT: If you want to continue fault-finding the rest of the PCB, click on ‘Skip’
SKIP_FAIL: #2
GOTO: #3

#2.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
test passed
CLICK_OK:




#3: PCB Program version check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BUILD
READLINE: MLPRO2  BUILD
Check the Returned result is current version as per TD037 PCB Programming Data Register.

Returned Version is = %BUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . no communication
PASS_FAIL: #3



#4: READVOLTS check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
READLINE: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
Returned Version is = %READVOLTS%
RANGE: %READVOLTS% 1200 50					// PASS if TEMP is between 12050 and 12150
IF:
GOTO: #4.1: // if line 30 and 31 results match goto next test
.
The returned result is NOT as exected, investigate the fault and click RETRY to repeat the test.
.
.
The expected result is =  greater than 10V 
IMPORTANT: Test has FAILED                Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED
COMMENT: If you want to continue fault-finding the rest of the PCB, click on ‘Skip’
SKIP_FAIL: #4
GOTO: #5

#4.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
test passed
CLICK_OK:



#5: Test complete:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
SAVE_LOG:
// turn off any LEDs still on: 

// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

